## This lab will cover setting up port forwarding and jump boxes

### Remove static route from rw01
- on our rw01
  - sudo ip route del 172.16.50.0/29

### Port Forwarding
- Now we are going to add a NAT destination rule (a.k.a. port forwarding) so that any port 80 traffic coming to our firewall's WAN/eth0 interface will be forwarded on to web01. 
  - The destination port refers to the port received by eth0 on fw1
  - The inbound interface is eth0/WAN
  - The address received is "translated" and forwarded to web01 port 80
- To do this:
  - set nat destination rule 10 description "HTTP->WEB01"
  - set nat destination rule 10 destination port 80
  - set nat destination rule 10 inbound-interface name eth0
  - set nat destination rule 10 protocol tcp
  - set nat destination rule 10 translation address 172.16.50.3
  - set nat destination rule 10 translation port 80

### The Jump Box
- go to hardware in proxmox and change network adapter to our DMZ
- Add a new user
  - sudo adduser azrael
- Add our new user to sudoers group
  - sudo usermod -aG sudo azrael
- Change hostname
  - sudo hostnamectl set-hostname jump-azrael
- Using the netplan yaml file configure
  - addresses: 172.16.50.4/29
  - nameservers: 172.16.50.2
  - routes: - to: 0.0.0.0/0 via: 172.16.50.2
- sudo netplan apply

### Firewalls and SSH
- make a rule so that our fw only listens on LAN for ssh connections
  - set service ssh listen-address 172.16.150.2

### Key Generation on rw01
- On rw01 we will create a dedicated keypair that will only be used for ssh access to jump
  - ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096 -f ~/.ssh/jump_key -C "SSH key for jump server access"
### Passwordless User on jump
- First we create new passwordless user
  - sudo adduser jump-azrael-passless --disabled-password
- Now set up SSH authorized keys for the user
  - sudo mkdir -p /home/jump-azrael-passless/.ssh
  - sudo chmod 700 /home/jump-azrael-passless/.ssh
  - sudo chown jump-azrael-passless:jump-azrael-passless /home/jump-azrael-passless/.ssh
- We need to add a temp rule to our firewall now to allow scp from rw to jump
  - set firewall ipv4 name WAN-to-DMZ rule 999 action accept
  - set firewall ipv4 name WAN-to-DMZ rule 999 protocol tcp
  - set firewall ipv4 name WAN-to-DMZ rule 999 source address 10.0.17.20
  - set firewall ipv4 name WAN-to-DMZ rule 999 destination address 172.16.50.4
  - set firewall ipv4 name WAN-to-DMZ rule 999 destination port 22
- delete this rule once done

- Copy the public key from rw01 to jump
- on rw01
  - scp ~/.ssh/jump_key.pub azrael@172.16.50.4:/tmp/
  - ssh azrael@172.16.50.4
- on jump
  - sudo mv /tmp/jump_key.pub /home/jump-azrael-passless/.ssh/authorized_keys
  - sudo chmod 600 /home/jump-azrael-passless/.ssh/authorized_keys
  - sudo chown jump-azrael-passless:jump-azrael-passless /home/jump-azrael-passless/.ssh/authorized_keys

### Create NAT destination rule (port forwarding) on fw01
- set nat destination rule 20 description "SSH->JUMP"
- set nat destination rule 20 destination port 22
- set nat destination rule 20 inbound-interface name eth0
- set nat destination rule 20 protocol tcp
- set nat destination rule 20 translation address 172.16.50.4
- set nat destination rule 20 translation port 22
- commit -> save

### Adjust WAN-to-DMZ firewall to allow SSH from WAN to jump
- set firewall ipv4 name WAN-to-DMZ rule 20 action accept
- set firewall ipv4 name WAN-to-DMZ rule 20 protocol tcp
- set firewall ipv4 name WAN-to-DMZ rule 20 destination address 172.16.50.4
- set firewall ipv4 name WAN-to-DMZ rule 20 destination port 22
- set firewall ipv4 name WAN-to-DMZ rule 20 description "Allow SSH from WAN to jump"
- commit -> save

### Create an account for the internal admin
- sudo adduser azrael-adm
- sudo usermod -aG sudo azrael-adm

### Wazuh agent on Jump
- download most recent agent package on mgmt01, then ->
  - scp wazuh-agent_4.14.3-1_amd64.deb azrael-adm@172.16.50.4:/tmp/
  - ssh azrael-adm@172.16.50.4
  - cd /tmp
  - sudo WAZUH_MANAGER='172.16.200.10' dpkg -i wazuh-agent_4.14.3-1_amd64.deb
  - sudo systemctl start wazuh-agent
  - sudo systemctl enable wazuh-agent
  - sudo systemctl status wazuh-agent
